# 128 - §2: assignment with no `let` and no existing binding anywhere is a
# runtime Name error, at the Assign statement's line (2). The line printed
# before it is kept (§3), which is what makes this a two-part assertion rather
# than just "it errored".
#
# Wording is error.rs's `assign_unbound`, which is deliberately distinct from a
# bad READ (`undefined variable`) so the two failures are tellable apart. This
# case originally cited bead .39's table, which §6a/.55 superseded; corrected
# under bead .71 after group B graded 130/131 and this was the one failure.
--- source
print "before";
y = 1;
print "never";
--- expect
before
error: Name at line 2: assignment to undefined variable 'y'
